## Why This Is Asked
This question probes multi-tenant CNF provenance at scale, including per-tenant keys, drift detection, rollback, and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped key management
- Per-tenant SBOMs and provenance enforcement
- ImagePolicyWebhook + OPA constraints
- Drift detection and tenant-aware rollback
- Observability: metrics, traces, audit logs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify image provenance per tenant
async function verifyProvenance(imageRef, tenant) {
  const sigOk = await cosign.verify(imageRef, { key: `kms://${tenant}-key` });
  const sbom = await fetchSBOM(imageRef);
  if (sbom.tenant !== tenant) throw new Error('Tenant SBOM mismatch');
  return sigOk;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate tenant keys without downtime?
- How would you test drift detection across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical security design in a service-mMesh context, focusing on per-tenant egress control, runtime policy evaluation, and rollout strategy—uncovering depth beyond static docs.

## Key Concepts
- SPIFFE IDs and workload labeling for tenant isolation
- Istio EgressGateway + AuthorizationPolicy for egress enforcement
- OPA-backed policy store for dynamic per-tenant allowlists
- Observable tenant badge surface in gateway status and rollout signals

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example JS-like policy evaluation (illustrative only)
const canAccess = (tenant, endpoint) => {
  const allowlist = {
    'tenant-a': ['telemetry.example.com','updates.example.com'],
    'tenant-b': ['telemetry.example.org']
  }
  return (allowlist[tenant] || []).includes(endpoint)
}
```
